 # Chunk-based Voxel Rendering Pipeline
 
-Also called: Baking geometry into VBOs, Batched Voxel Rendering Pipeline, Chunk VBOs, Chunk-based Voxel Rendering
+Also called: Baking geometry into VBOs, Batched Voxel Rendering Pipeline, Chunk VBOs
 
 ## Overview
-The Chunk-based Voxel Rendering Pipeline aggregates individual voxel cubes into larger static mesh batches (chunks) and uploads them to GPU Vertex Buffer Objects (VBOs) to overcome the high overhead of instancing small, per-cube geometry [S1, S3, unofficial]. It separates the visibility processing (handled by an octree or spatial structure) from the rendering loop, which simply traverses a list of active chunk VBOs [S1, unofficial]. This approach eliminates hidden faces and reduces draw calls, making it suitable for high-throughput rendering where GPU fill rate and generation bottlenecks are critical [S1, unofficial].
+The Chunk-based Voxel Rendering Pipeline aggregates individual voxel cubes into larger static mesh batches (chunks) and uploads them to GPU Vertex Buffer Objects (VBOs) to overcome the high overhead of instancing small, per-cube geometry [S1, unofficial]. It separates visibility processing (handled by an octree or spatial structure) from the rendering loop, which simply traverses a list of active chunk VBOs [S1, unofficial]. This approach eliminates hidden faces and reduces draw calls, making it suitable for high-throughput rendering where GPU fill rate and generation bottlenecks are critical [S1, unofficial].
 
